===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|fleeting|-ly<id:adverbial>|text=+|tree=1}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[fleeting]] manner; [[transient]]ly.
#: {{co|en|appear '''fleetingly'''}}
#: {{co|en|glimpse '''fleetingly'''}}
#: {{co|en|'''fleetingly''' visible}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1957|author=w:Bernard Malamud|title={{w|The Assistant (novel)|The Assistant}}|location=New York|publisher=Farrar, Straus and Cudahy|chapter=1|page=8|url=https://archive.org/details/assistantnovel00mala
|passage=He wished '''fleetingly''' that he could once more be out in the open, as when he was a boy—never in the house, but the sound of the blustery wind frightened him.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=circ. 1965|author=w:Mario Puzo|title=The Godfather
|passage=She took the holy water on her fingertips and made the sign of the cross, '''fleetingly''' touched her wet fingertips to her parched lips. Candles flickered redly before the saints, the Christ on his cross. Kay genuflected before entering her row and then knelt on the hard wooden rail of the pew to wait for her call to Communion.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2017
|month=November
|author=w:N. K. Jemisin; w:Mac Walters
|chapter=1
|title={{w|Mass_Effect:_Andromeda_(book_series)#Initiation|Mass Effect Andromeda: Initiation}}
|url=https://archive.org/details/masseffectandrom0000jemi/
|edition=1st
|genre=Science Fiction
|publisher=w:Titan Books
|ISBN=978-1785651601
|OCLC=999444073
|page=32
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/masseffectandrom0000jemi/page/32/
|text= “I’m not sure I understand why we have to send a quadrillion-credit mission to another galaxy.”<br>He looked '''fleetingly''' amused. “Quintillion... and we don’t have a choice, Harper. Any of us, really, but humanity especially.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021|author=Stathis Gourgouris|title=Dream Nation
|passage=And so the followers of Seferis, although they inherit a method, practice an unmethod, a methodological void. Or, to put it more precisely: although not forced to travel '''fleetingly''' from place to place, they travel anyway—to nonplaces, {{...}}}}

